meta {
  name: Get versions matrix - incompatible connector slug
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/opencti/versions-matrix?version=6.260807.0&connector_slugs=sekoia
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  version: 6.260807.0
  connector_slugs: sekoia
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 409
}

docs {
  A requested slug that is known but has no version (not even a historical
  fallback) compatible with the requested OpenCTI version is rejected with
  409 (the slug exists, it just conflicts with the resolved version).
  GoogleTi requires OpenCTI >= 8.260901.0, which is above every
  registered OpenCTI version, to force this case.
  
  Response: { "code": 409, "message": "Incompatible connector slug(s) for OpenCTI version 7.260807.0: GoogleTi" }
  
  Note: `version` must itself be a *registered* OpenCTI version (see
  GetVersionsMatrixUnregisteredVersion.bru) — an arbitrary/made-up version
  like "1.0.0" is rejected as "Unknown opencti version" before slug
  compatibility is even checked.
}
